<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kircholm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1605">1605</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-swedish-war-1600-1611">Polish–Swedish War (1600–1611)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kircholm was fought in 1605 near Riga between the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> and a larger Swedish army. Commonwealth forces under Jan Karol Chodkiewicz, led by the winged hussar cavalry, won a crushing victory. It is regarded as one of the greatest successes of the Commonwealth's army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kircholm.jpg" alt="Battle of Kircholm" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Snayers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pieter_Snayers_-_Battle_of_Kircholm,_1605.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>At the <b>Battle of Kircholm</b> in 1605, a Commonwealth force of some 3,600 men, its striking power provided by hussars, routed a Swedish army of around 11,000 in a short and decisive engagement.</blockquote><a href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>From 1600 Sweden and Poland-Lithuania fought over Livonia; the Polish victory at <b>Kircholm</b> in 1605 delayed Swedish conquest, but Gustav II Adolf took Riga in 1621.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-livonia">Duchy of Livonia</a></li></ul></section>
